The package as a whole is released under the MIT license (file LICENSE).

Most rules in the data file inst/extdata/rules.bin were computed by the package author.
Some descend from rules published by others; the catalog inst/extdata/index.tsv (column
"origin") says which, and ruleinfo() reports it at run time. The file NOTICE.md of the
source repository (https://github.com/NittanyLion/quadriceps-r) gives the full account.

The lepos rules for d = 2, p = 77 and d = 3, p = 27, 29, ..., 45 descend from the rules of
M. Diallo and Z. A. Worku, "High-order symmetric positive interior quadrature rules on two
and three dimensional domains", arXiv:2601.14488 (2026), data at
https://github.com/mdiallo-fula/SymmetricPositiveInteriorCubatures.jl, released under the
MIT license. They are modified copies in the sense of that license, whose notice follows:

